{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# Product intent\n2\t\n3\t## Purpose\n4\t\n5\tConversation Ledger preserves durable, inspectable records of visible\n6\tconversations between people and coding agents. It is a general conversation\n7\tprovenance primitive, not an intent-analysis product. Downstream consumers may\n8\tuse its records as evidence about why a repository changed, but the ledger must\n9\tnot impose that interpretation.\n10\t\n11\tThe record must remain useful to consumers beyond a single tool: cross-CLI\n12\tcontinuity, archival/export, code attribution, review, and later intent\n13\tretrieval are all valid independent uses.\n14\t\n15\t## Behavioral commitments\n16\t\n17\t- Preserve source material and provenance; do not silently rewrite history.\n18\t- Preserve exact visible turns before creating optional derived views.\n19\t- Retain enough provenance for consumers to determine applicability without\n20\t  treating any record as timeless truth.\n21\t- Record the repository, branch, commit, worktree state, author, timestamps,\n22\t  and capture mechanism with each artifact whenever available.\n23\t- Keep storage out of ordinary working-tree status views while retaining normal\n24\t  Git durability and shareability.\n25\t- Make sharing, retention, redaction, and deletion deliberate user choices.\n26\t\n27\t## Non-goals for the foundation\n28\t\n29\t- Deciding which historical statement is correct or intended.\n30\t- Summarizing, ranking, embedding, or otherwise interpreting conversations.\n31\t- Controlling an agent, enforcing a workflow, or orchestrating agents.\n32\t- Decrypting, interpreting, or reproducing reasoning the provider hides.\n33\t  Visible reasoning is recorded when exposed; reasoning withheld behind\n34\t  provider ciphertext (0.10.0+) is preserved losslessly as opaque raw state\n35\t  for a capable downstream consumer to decrypt later, but the ledger itself\n36\t  never attempts to read or reconstruct it, and stores nothing that would let\n37\t  it reproduce a native agent session on its own. As of 0.19.0 that covers\n38\t  ciphertext embedded inside another payload too — an inter-agent message's\n39\t  `encrypted_content` blocks ride alongside the visible turn as a sealed\n40\t  sibling — so \"preserved, never read\" is now the rule everywhere rather than\n41\t  the rule for standalone reasoning items only.\n42\t\n43\tThose belong to clients such as Turnbridge and Intent Recall, not to this core\n44\tstorage layer.\n45\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jii9V2SXQiF335a4ZfvALx","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"redaction-ux","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger-worktrees/redaction-ux","head":"fb4df15a7bdebc38ca45aa5ad908b0fcb411d13c","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:b8bc0200-5312-42a4-9c54-a116d8d4a925","seq":115},"id":"ev1-c33e50f356f2bbba93d38a6aa4c47f037ab8ecf5aff69b911f38135f56e535a3","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-12T02:17:14.118Z","producer":{"session_id":"b8bc0200-5312-42a4-9c54-a116d8d4a925","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.228","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger-worktrees/redaction-ux","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"redaction-ux","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"1\t# Product intent\n2\t\n3\t## Purpose\n4\t\n5\tConversation Ledger preserves durable, inspectable records of visible\n6\tconversations between people and coding agents. It is a general conversation\n7\tprovenance primitive, not an intent-analysis product. Downstream consumers may\n8\tuse its records as evidence about why a repository changed, but the ledger must\n9\tnot impose that interpretation.\n10\t\n11\tThe record must remain useful to consumers beyond a single tool: cross-CLI\n12\tcontinuity, archival/export, c