.ts:146-154`)** — `high-entropy`, `/\\b[A-Za-z0-9+/_=-]{24,}\\b/g`, `entropyGated: true`. Gated in the scanner (`scan.ts:67-74`) by: tier must be paranoid, not pure hex (`PURE_HEX_RE`, git SHAs), not containing `[REDACTED:`, and `shannonEntropy(matchText) &gt;= 4.0`.\n\n`rulesForTier` (`rules.ts:163-167`) is cumulative: capture ⊂ standard ⊂ paranoid. Capture-time application **skips `entropyGated` rules** (`apply.ts:33`).\n\n### Traversal and exemptions\n- `walkStrings(value, path, visit)` (`apply.ts:120-135`) deep-walks string leaves only (never object keys), producing JSON-pointer-ish paths like `content/blocks/0/text`, `raw/data/message/content/0/text`. Shared by both `redactDraft` and `scanEvents` so they can't drift.\n- Scanned surfaces: `event.content` (path root `content`) and `event.raw.data` (root `raw/data`) — `scan.ts:89-90`, `apply.ts:165-168`.\n- **One exemption**: `isExemptFromRedaction(kind, path)` (`apply.ts:107-109`) → `kind === \"reasoning\" &amp;&amp; path.endsWith(\"/encrypted_content\")`. Provider ciphertext must stay byte-exact for replay; a coincidental match would silently corrupt it. Sibling fields (`summary`) are still scanned — tested at `src/test/scan.test.ts:142-171`.\n- `overlapsPlaceholder` (`scan.ts:33-40`) suppresses findings that land inside an existing `[REDACTED:…]` span.\n\n### Fingerprints\n`sha256Hex(matchText).slice(0, 12)` — 12 hex chars, computed identically in `scan.ts:80` and `apply.ts:35`/`apply.ts:66`. This is the join key between a finding, a `[REDACTED:...]` placeholder, and an allowlist entry.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Review flow\n\n### The contentless report (this is the design centerpiece)\n\n```ts\n// src/redact/scan.ts:111-114\nexport function formatFinding(f: Finding): string {\n  const where = `${f.path}@${f.start}`;\n  return `${f.eventId.slice(0, 16)}  ${f.conversation ?? \"-\"}  ${f.occurred_at}  ${f.rule}  ${where}  [${f.fingerprint}]`;\n}\n```\n\nThe 20-line comment above it (`scan.ts:96-110`) is the rationale: an earlier version printed ~20 chars of masked context, but *the context is what tripped the rule*, so reports captured into the next conversation re-seeded findings that `cledger allow` couldn't durably clear. Coordinates match no secret rule.\n\n`findingGuidance(eventIds)` (`scan.ts:186-204`) is appended to every report and splits its audience explicitly:\n\n```\n  If you are a HUMAN: inspect it in a plain terminal, outside any agent:\n      cledger inspect &lt;first-16-chars&gt;\n  ...\n  If you are an AGENT: stop here and hand this to the human. Do not run\n  cledger inspect, cledger export, or otherwise read the flagged content —\n  it would be captured into this conversation and re-seed the finding.\n```\n\n### The `.txt` review file — `cledger inspect`\n\nWriter: `cmdInspect`, `src/cli.ts:452-524`.\n\n- **Guard 1** (`cli.ts:459-468`): refuses if `inAgentSession()` (`scan.ts:174-179`, matches any env var `/^(CLAUDECODE|CLAUDE_CODE|CODEX_)/`). `--force` overrides; message says \"almost always the wrong call\". Exits 2.\n- **Guard 2**: writes to a file, not stdout, unless `--stdout`.\n\n```ts\n// src/cli.ts:513-523\nconst dir = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), \"cledger-inspect-\"));\nconst out = join(dir, `${prefix.slice(0, 16)}.txt`);\nawait writeFile(out, body, { mode: 0o600 });\nprocess.stderr.write(\n  `${findings.length} finding(s) written to:\\n  ${out}\\n\\n` +\n    \"Open it in an editor, then delete it. Re-run with --reveal to include the\\n\" +\n    \"matched text itself, or --context N to widen the surrounding text.\\n\",\n);\n```\n\n**Location:** `$TMPDIR/cledger-inspect-XXXXXX/&lt;event-id-prefix-16&gt;.txt`, mode 0600, outside the repo, **never cleaned up** — the user is told to delete it.\n\n**File format** — header from `cli.ts:499-507`, then one block per finding from `renderFinding` (`scan.ts:142-163`):\n\n```\ncledger inspect — N finding(s) in M event(s)\ncontext: 400 chars each side | matched text: masked\n                                                       (blank)\nThis file contains raw conversation content and possibly a real secret.\nDelete it when you are done, and do not paste it into an agent session.\n\nrule:        keyword-assignment\nfingerprint: 0f21be5a42c9\nevent:       ev1-&lt;full 64 hex&gt;\nconversation:&lt;id or \" -\"&gt;\noccurred_at: 2026-08-11T...\nlocation:    content/blocks/0/text, chars 120-145 of 4000\nmatch:       25 chars, masked (pass --reveal to show)\n\n…[N chars before]…\n&lt;400 chars of real context&gt;&lt;redacted&gt;&lt;400 chars of real context&gt;\n…[N chars after]…\n```\n\n- Context default **400 chars each side**, `--context N` (`cli.ts:473`; validated non-negative at `cli.ts:474-477`).\n- Match masked with the literal `&lt;redacted&gt;` (`MATCH_MARKER`, `scan.ts:43`) unless `--reveal`.\n- Truncation is disclosed, never silent (`scan.ts:160`; tested `scan.test.ts:342`).\n- Handles a stale finding: `\"string no longer present in event ... (event rewritten since the scan?)\"` (`scan.ts:145`).\n\n**There is no command that consumes the human's verdict from the file.** The file is read-only output. The human then types one of two separate commands by hand.\n\n### Verdict commands\n\n**\"False positive\" → `cledger allow &lt;fingerprint...&gt;`** — `cmdAllow`, `src/cli.ts:526-534`. Accepts N positional fingerprints, no validation of format or existence, prints `allowlisted N fingerprint(s)`.\n\nAllowlist file — `src/redact/scan.ts:211-239`:\n- Path: `&lt;git-common-dir&gt;/conversation-ledger/allowlist.json` (`allowlistPath`, `scan.ts:215-217`) — i.e. `.git/conversation-ledger/allowlist.json`, shared across worktrees via `repo.commonDir`.\n- Format: `{\"fingerprints\": [\"0f21be5a42c9\", ...]}` sorted, 2-space indented, trailing newline.\n- Load fails soft to empty set on missing/malformed (`scan.ts:220-229`).\n- `addToAllowlist` is additive/deduping (`scan.ts:231-239`).\n- Applied via `filterFindings(findings, allowlist)` (`scan.ts:207-209`) — used by `cmdScan` (`cli.ts:427`) and `runScanGate` (`store.ts:817`), **not** by `cledger inspect`.\n- **Live dogfood evidence**: this repo's own `.git/conversation-ledger/allowlist.json` currently holds **29 fingerprints**.\n\n**\"Real secret\" → `cledger redact &lt;event-id-prefix&gt; (--pattern REGEX | --all) [--reason TEXT]`** — `cmdRedact` (`cli.ts:536-588`) → `redactEvent` (`store.ts:1112-1295`). Note the UX asymmetry: the human must retype the secret as a regex, having just read it out of the `.txt` file. On success it prints the fingerprints, the companion event id, and a paragraph about notes-history severing vs. object residue (`cli.ts:568-581`).\n\n**Known-secrets list** — `src/redact/known-secrets.ts`, opt-in via `{\"redact\":{\"knownSecrets\":true}}`:\n- Path: `&lt;git-common-dir&gt;/conversation-ledger/known-secrets.json` (`known-secrets.ts:43-45`).\n- Format: `{\"values\": [\"&lt;plaintext secret&gt;\", ...]}` sorted, mode `0o600` (`STORE_MODE`, `known-secrets.ts:29`), chmod-repaired on every write (`known-secrets.ts:80-85`).\n- Entries added **only** by `cledger redact --pattern` (`store.ts:1166-1169` collects via `collectMatches`; `store.ts:1228-1233` persists). `--all` never feeds it. Values `&lt; 8` chars dropped (`MIN_VALUE_LENGTH`, `known-secrets.ts:37`); file is never created if nothing survives filtering.\n- Consumed at capture as an `ExtraValueGroup{ruleId:\"known-secret\"}` (`store.ts:179-182`), exact-string scrubbed longest-first (`apply.ts:56-74`, sorted `apply.ts:150-152`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Push gating\n\n**There is no `cledger push`.** The push surfaces are `cledger sync [--push]` and `cledger transport-push` (the pre-push hook entrypoint).\n\n### The gate — `src/store.ts:792-834`\n\nScan scope is exactly what the push would carry, minus what the remote already has:\n\n```ts\n// src/store.ts:798-818\nconst remoteIds = await remoteNoteIds(repo, remote);\nconst localEvents: EvidenceEvent[] = [];\nfor (const anchor of anchors ?? (await listAnchors(repo))) {\n  localEvents.push(...(await readNoteEvents(repo, anchor)));\n}\nlocalEvents.push(...(await readPending(repo)));\nconst candidates = remoteIds ? localEvents.filter((e) =&gt; !remoteIds.has(e.id)) : localEvents;\nif (candidates.length === 0) return;\nconst findings = filterFindings(scanEvents(candidates, tier), await loadAllowlist(repo));\nif (findings.length === 0) return;\n```\n\nThen the blocked-user UX (`store.ts:820-833`) — **all on stderr**:\n\n```\ncledger sync: blocked — 3 potential secret(s) across 2 event(s) not yet on origin\n\n  ev1-4f9a3c...  claude-code:3f9a  2026-08-11T...  keyword-assignment  content/blocks/0/text@120  [0f21be5a42c9]\n  ...\n\n&lt;findingGuidance block — HUMAN/AGENT split&gt;\n\nRemediate, then re-run sync:\n  cledger redact &lt;event-id&gt;     rewrite the event and remove the secret\n  cledger allow &lt;fingerprint&gt;   mark a fingerprint as a known false positive\n  cledger sync --no-scan        skip this gate for this sync only\n```\n\nthen `throw new ScanBlockedError(findings.length)` (`store.ts:734-738`), whose message is `cledger sync: push blocked — N potential secret(s) found (see report above)`.\n\nGate invocation and the disable path — `store.ts:866-871`:\n```ts\nconst scanDisabled = opts.skipScan === true || config.scan?.tier === \"off\";\nif (!scanDisabled) {\n  const tier: \"standard\" | \"paranoid\" =\n    opts.paranoid === true || config.scan?.tier === \"paranoid\" ? \"paranoid\" : \"standard\";\n  await runScanGate(repo, remote, tier, anchors);\n}\n```\nThe throw happens *before* the actual `git push` (`store.ts:877-881`), so nothing leaves the machine. Fetch/merge, if it already ran, is left in place.\n\n### Enforcement points, complete list\n\n1. **Pre-push git hook** (default on) — installed on first capture by `ensureTransport` → `ensurePrePushHook` (`src/transport.ts:154-226`). Hook body at `transport.ts:74-94`, written to `&lt;commonDir&gt;/hooks/pre-push`, guarded by `CLEDGER_INTERNAL` to avoid recursion, piping git's pre-push stdin to `cledger transport-push \"$1\"`. Backs off with a one-time warning when `core.hooksPath` is set or the existing hook is not a shell script (`transport.ts:178-188`, `212-221`).\n2. **`transportPush`** (`store.ts:937-970`) — the policy layer. Default: a finding holds back **only the ledger**, the code push proceeds:\n   ```ts\n   if (err instanceof ScanBlockedError) {\n     if (config.transport?.strict === true) throw err;\n     process.stderr.write(\n       \"cledger: conversation records were held back from this push (potential secrets — \" +\n         \"see report above); your code push continues. Run `cledger sync` to review and \" +\n         \"remediate.\\n\");\n     return { pushed: false, held: true };\n   }\n   ```\n   With `transport.strict`, the CLI catches the rethrow and exits 1 (`cli.ts:407-412`), printing `cledger: entire push blocked (transport.strict is enabled)` — git then aborts the whole push. Any *other* error warns and lets the push proceed (`store.ts:965-969`; hook must never make `git push` flaky).\n3. **`cledger scan`** — CI gate, exit 1 (`cli.ts:438`).\n4. **`cledger redact` pre-push gate** — `assertNotYetShared` (`store.ts:1067-1099`) refuses to redact an event already on origin, and **fails closed** when origin is unreachable (`RedactAfterShareError`, `store.ts:745-753`). Both messages are multi-paragraph explanations printed verbatim by `cli.ts:554-558`.\n5. **Capture time** — masking only; never blocks or notifies.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Config surfaces\n\nLoaded by `loadConfig(repoRoot)` — `src/redact/config.ts:108-129`. Two files:\n- `~/.config/cledger/config.json` (global)\n- `&lt;repoRoot&gt;/.cledger.json` (repo; wins)\n\n**Merge is per top-level section, not per key** (`config.ts:117-121`): `const redact = override.redact ?? base.redact`. This is a known, documented bug — README.md:384-395 (\"Config sections replace rather than merge, and it fails open\"): a repo `.cledger.json` with any `redact` key silently reverts a globally-enabled `redact.knownSecrets`. Malformed/non-object config warns to stderr and falls back to defaults (`config.ts:75-100`).\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Where read | Effect |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `enabled` | bool | `true` | `store.ts:166` | `false` = appendEvents is a total no-op |\n| `redact.capture` | bool | `true` | `config.ts:137` | `false` → `captureRules` returns `[]`, no capture masking at all |\n| `redact.env` | bool | `false` | `store.ts:183` | scrub exact `process.env` + `&lt;repo&gt;/.env` values (`collectEnvValues`, `config.ts:187-200`) |\n| `redact.knownSecrets` | bool | `false` | `store.ts:179`, `store.ts:1128` | enable the learned-value store |\n| `redact.patterns` | `{id?, pattern}[]` | `[]` | `config.ts:139-153` | extra capture rules; invalid regex **skipped silently**; auto-id `user-pattern-&lt;i&gt;` |\n| `scan.tier` | `\"standard\"\\|\"paranoid\"\\|\"off\"` | `\"standard\"` | `store.ts:866-869` | `\"off\"` disables the push gate |\n| `transport.hook` | bool | `true` | `transport.ts:172`, `store.ts:943` | install/run the pre-push hook |\n| `transport.strict` | bool | `false` | `store.ts:957` | escalate a finding from \"hold the ledger\" to \"abort the whole git push\" |\n| `transport.fetchRefspec` | bool | `true` | `transport.ts:232` | add the ledger fetch refspec |\n| `reanchor.auto` | bool | `true` | `store.ts:548` | (not redaction) |\n| `reanchor.forge` | bool | `true` | `cli.ts:634` | (not redaction) |\n\n**Env vars:** only two, neither a config knob.\n- `CLEDGER_INTERNAL` — set by `sync()` around the ledger push (`store.ts:874-885`) and checked by the hook script (`transport.ts:82`) to prevent recursion.\n- `CLAUDECODE` / `CLAUDE_CODE*` / `CODEX_*` — read by `inAgentSession` (`scan.ts:174-179`) to refuse `cledger inspect`. Note: **no marker for opencode, gemini-cli, or qwen-code**, all of which are supported adapters — the guard has a coverage gap.\n- Tests isolate `$HOME` at module load (`src/test/helpers.ts:26-34`) precisely so a developer's global `knownSecrets: true` can't change test behavior.\n\nCLI flags relevant to redaction: `sync --no-scan`, `sync --paranoid`; `scan --paranoid`, `scan --all|--rev`; `inspect --context N --reveal --stdout --force`; `redact --pattern|--all --reason`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Test fixtures\n\n**Convention: split secrets, reassemble at runtime.** `src/test/fixtures/secret-corpus.json` stores each fake secret as `secret_parts: [...]` split mid-token, with a `{SECRET}` placeholder in `context`. Rationale at `src/test/secret-corpus.test.ts:30-36`:\n\n&gt; Fixture entries store each fake secret as `secret_parts` (split mid-token) with a `{SECRET}` placeholder in the context, so no literal token bytes exist in the repository — otherwise secret scanners (GitHub push protection, gitleaks over the source tree) flag the corpus itself.\n\nReassembly: `src/test/secret-corpus.test.ts:43-50`. Corpus: **27 positives** (2-3 per capture rule) and **9 negatives** (UUID, git SHA, sha256, base64 PNG, `\"version\": \"1.2.3\"`, `sk-anthropic` prose near-miss, `THEME=dark-mode-enabled`, a GitHub URL, a JS code block with `Bearer ${token}`). Counts are asserted (`secret-corpus.test.ts:57-58`), so adding a fixture requires bumping the numbers.\n\n**Second convention: generated fake secrets.** `src/test/redact.test.ts:13-53` — `chars(charset, n)` builds deterministic filler, `FAKE_SECRETS` maps each capture rule id to one format-valid fake, `fakeSecret(id)` throws if a rule has no fixture. A loop at `redact.test.ts:57-71` asserts *every* capture rule has one and redacts it.\n\n**Third convention: unrecognizable-shape secrets for redact tests.** `\"hunter2xK9aa\"` (12 chars, no prefix) recurs throughout `redact-command.test.ts` and `known-secrets.test.ts`, deliberately chosen so the capture tier leaves it raw and the test exercises the manual path — annotated at `redact-command.test.ts:30` and `known-secrets.test.ts:48`.\n\n**External oracle:** `secret-corpus.test.ts:139-182` shells out to `gitleaks detect --no-git` over the redacted outputs, skipping the test if gitleaks is absent. Design doc layer B (`WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:432-435`): external scanners are a *test oracle only*, never vendored into the runtime path.\n\n**Fixtures that have historically tripped the scanner** — documented in the roadmap rather than in code:\n- `README.md:493-506`: this repo's own allowlist picked up two `keyword-assignment` fingerprints from `const secret = fakeSecret(\"github-token\")` — a rule-id label, not a credential.\n- `README.md:507-524`: the *write-up* of that false positive, quoted into an `intent-recall` design conversation, produced 6 new `keyword-assignment` findings in a different repo. The doc's own conclusion: the rule wants a \"discussion vs. assignment\" discriminator (prose/markdown context vs. code block), not more allowlisting.\n- `scan.test.ts:56-73` locks in the negative cases from dogfooding cledger's own source: type annotations (`secret: string`), template interpolation (`${secret.slice(i, i + 6)}`), interface fields.\n- `scan.test.ts:75-89` locks in the positives that must still fire.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Core thesis / threat model / architecture\n\n**Purpose** (`docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md:3-13`): \"a general conversation provenance primitive, not an intent-analysis product.\" Behavioral commitments include \"Preserve source material and provenance; **do not silently rewrite history**\" and \"Make sharing, retention, **redaction**, and deletion **deliberate user choices**\" (`PRODUCT_INTENT.md:17,25`). Non-goals: summarizing, ranking, interpreting, controlling an agent (`PRODUCT_INTENT.md:27-32`).\n\n**Threat model, verbatim** (`docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:411-417`):\n\n&gt; Visible tool output can contain secrets. **The trust boundary is transport**: native transcripts already sit in plaintext on the capturing machine, so redaction protects the *shared* record, not the local disk. But once a secret reaches a note, removal is expensive (the notes ref's own history retains prior blobs), so prevention layers run at capture and the last checkpoint runs at sync. Content hashes (event ids) make accidental mutation detectable.\n\nThis single sentence justifies: plaintext `known-secrets.json` under `.git/`, the local reflog residue after redaction, and the refusal to redact post-push.\n\n**Six redaction layers A-F** (`WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:419-496`, mirrored in `README.md:232-253`): A capture patterns (on), B external scanners as test oracle only, C env masking (off), D user patterns (config), E sync scan (on, tiered), F known-secret learning (off).\n\n**Load-bearing invariants any redesign must respect:**\n1. *Capture-tier rules must be near-zero-false-positive* — a false positive silently rewrites the record, violating the preservation commitment (`rules.ts:2-8`, `TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:429-431`). The \"make capture a superset of scan\" idea was **explicitly considered and rejected** (`README.md:613-618`).\n2. *Determinism* — capture-time redaction must be a pure function of source content + versioned ruleset, or rescans duplicate events (`TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:507-510`). Layers C and F break this on purpose and pay in id churn.\n3. *Id stability under redaction* — `redactEvent` pins `original.id`; the CRITICAL comment at `store.ts:1177-1191` explains that recomputing it would let a later rescan resurrect the plaintext under the old id. Guarded by an explicit drift check (`store.ts:1202-1207`) and by the dedup test at `redact-command.test.ts:79-92`.\n4. *Reads never walk notes history* — only the tip tree is authoritative, because ancestry retains pre-redaction bodies (`TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:685-696`).\n5. *Redacted copy always wins dedup* — `redactionDepth` outranks `recorded_at` and byte-compare (`store.ts:350`, README.md:549-561).\n6. **\"Self-referential failures are now this project's characteristic bug family\"** (`README.md:397-408`) — the standing tripwire: \"ask what happens when that output is itself captured.\" Four known members, three fail silently, two fail open.\n\n**Architecture:** append-only JSONL evidence events, one canonical-JSON event per line, in a git note per anchor commit under `refs/notes/conversation-ledger` (`store.ts:56-67`). 13 event kinds (`schema.ts:58-72`) incl. `redaction`, `supersession`, `re_anchor`; 4 are \"session machinery\" hidden from `log`/`show` by default (`schema.ts:82-87`). Sync = `cat_sort_uniq` union merge, conflict-free; fetch stages into `refs/notes/cledger-incoming` and is absorbed lazily at read time (`transport.ts:257-287`); push is branch-scoped via `resolveAnchors` and seeds a temp ref from the remote's tip so it strictly adds (`store.ts:670-704`). Local, rebuildable state (cursors, `pending.jsonl`, `allowlist.json`, `known-secrets.json`) lives in `&lt;commonDir&gt;/conversation-ledger/` — \"never the record of truth\" (`store.ts:77`, `scan.ts:219`).\n\n---\n\n## 7. CLI structure\n\n**Framework: none.** Hand-rolled. `src/cli.ts:147-166` is the entire arg parser (`--flag value` / `--flag` boolean; anything not `--`-prefixed is positional; no `=` support, no short flags, no subcommand grouping). Dispatch is a `switch` at `cli.ts:708-818`. Usage is one 79-line template literal (`cli.ts:56-134`). `main().catch()` prints `cledger: &lt;message&gt;` and exits 1 (`cli.ts:821-824`).\n\n**Commands (17):** `append`, `log`, `show`, `conversations`, `export`, `sync`, `transport-push`, `scan`, `inspect`, `allow`, `redact`, `re-anchor`, `renormalize`, `install`, `hook &lt;source&gt;`, `capture &lt;source&gt;`, `--version|--help`.\n\n**Interactive/TUI code: none exists.** No readline, no prompts, no color, no spinner, no ANSI escapes, zero runtime dependencies (`package.json` has only `@types/node` and `typescript` as devDeps; no `node_modules` bin surface beyond that). The only TTY awareness in the codebase is `process.stdin.isTTY !== true` at `cli.ts:398`, used purely to avoid blocking on stdin in a manual `transport-push`. Note `README.md:424-428` flags terminal-awareness as a *tension to resolve* for any output redesign, since CI depends on the current inline report.\n\n**Output conventions:**\n- **stdout = data** (log lines, JSONL, findings from `cledger scan`, `--help`, `--version`).\n- **stderr = narration, warnings, remediation guidance, and every redaction message** — including the entire blocked-push report (`store.ts:821-832`).\n- Note the split within scan: `cmdScan` writes finding *lines* to stdout (`cli.ts:432`) but guidance/summary to stderr (`cli.ts:434-437`), while `runScanGate` writes *everything* to stderr. Anything redesigning report output must reconcile these two.\n- Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 findings/failure, 2 usage error or agent-session refusal.\n- Long explanatory prose is embedded directly in the message strings (`store.ts:1085-1098`, `cli.ts:568-581`, `scan.ts:186-204`) — the project's house style is to explain *why* in the output, on the stated theory (`README.md:420-422`) that \"an agent that understands *why* will comply, where a bare 'don't look' invites a workaround.\"\n\n---\n\n## Lifecycle of one detected secret, capture → push\n\n- **Capture.** An adapter hook (e.g. `cledger hook claude-code`) builds an `EventDraft` and calls `appendEvents` (`store.ts:158`). `loadConfig` merges global + repo config (`config.ts:108`). If `enabled !== false`, `captureRules(config)` assembles the 13 capture rules + any `redact.patterns` (`config.ts:136`).\n- **Capture-time masking.** `redactDraft` (`apply.ts:143`) deep-walks `content` and `raw.data`, skipping `reasoning`/`encrypted_content`, scrubbing known-secret and env exact values first (longest-first), then applying the capture regexes. A hit becomes `[REDACTED:&lt;rule&gt;:&lt;fp12&gt;]` plus a `redactions[]` record. **Silent — the user is told nothing.** If the secret's shape isn't in the capture tier (e.g. a bare `password=hunter2…`), it lands verbatim in the note.\n- **Storage.** `finalizeEvent` computes the id from the *already-redacted* content, so the id is a pure function of redacted source; the JSONL line is written into the git note on HEAD (`store.ts:217-221`) or into `.git/conversation-ledger/pending.jsonl` if HEAD is unborn.\n- **Push attempt.** `git push` fires the installed pre-push hook (`transport.ts:74-94`), which pipes git's ref lines into `cledger transport-push` → `parsePrePushRefs` (`store.ts:907`) → `sync(repo, remote, \"push\", {scope: revs})`.\n- **Gate.** Unless `--no-scan` or `scan.tier: \"off\"`, `runScanGate` (`store.ts:792`) computes the push's anchor set, subtracts event ids already on the remote, runs `scanEvents` at standard (or paranoid) tier, and drops any fingerprint in `.git/conversation-ledger/allowlist.json`.\n- **Block.** A surviving finding prints a coordinates-only line per finding + the HUMAN/AGENT guidance + the three remediation commands, all to stderr, then throws `ScanBlockedError`. Default: only the ledger is held back and the code push completes; with `transport.strict`, the CLI exits 1 and git aborts the entire push. **Nothing reached the remote** (asserted at `scan.test.ts:199-203`).\n- **Human review.** The human runs `cledger inspect &lt;event-id-prefix&gt;` in a plain terminal. It refuses if any `CLAUDECODE`/`CODEX_*` env var is present. Otherwise it re-scans that one event (unfiltered by the allowlist), renders each finding with 400 chars of real context each side and the match shown as `&lt;redacted&gt;`, and writes it to `$TMPDIR/cledger-inspect-XXXX/&lt;prefix&gt;.txt` at mode 0600, printing only the path. `--reveal` includes the literal secret; `--context N` widens.\n- **Verdict — false positive.** `cledger allow &lt;fp&gt;` appends to `allowlist.json`; the next sync passes (`scan.test.ts:210-238`). Per-repo and per-fingerprint, so every downstream repo re-encounters the same false positive from scratch (`README.md:514-517`).\n- **Verdict — real secret.** `cledger redact &lt;prefix&gt; --pattern &lt;regex&gt;`. `assertNotYetShared` refuses if the event is on origin or origin is unreachable. Otherwise, under the repo lock: rewrite content/raw with `[REDACTED:manual:&lt;fp&gt;]`, **preserve the original id**, rewrite the note line, append a companion `redaction` event with `links: [{rel:\"redacts\", target}]`, and squash the notes ref to a single commit so the pre-redaction blob is unreachable from the ref (objects survive in the reflog until `gc` — the CLI says so explicitly).\n- **Learning (opt-in).** With `redact.knownSecrets`, `collectMatches` captures the exact plaintext and `addKnownSecrets` writes it to `known-secrets.json` (0600, ≥8 chars). Every future capture exact-matches it out under the `known-secret` rule id — closing the loop where a scan-caught, capture-missed value gets re-ingested each time you discuss fixing it.\n- **Re-push.** Sync runs the gate again; findings are gone, `pushScopedNotes` seeds from the remote tip, unions the scoped anchors in, and pushes.\n- **Deleting the review file is manual.** Nothing in the codebase ever removes `$TMPDIR/cledger-inspect-*`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>141524</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>42</tool_uses><duration_ms>337839</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","operation":"enqueue","sessionId":"b8bc0200-5312-42a4-9c54-a116d8d4a925","timestamp":"2026-08-12T02:19:11.143Z","type":"queue-operation"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-13T00:39:22.312Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"activity_type":"queue-operation","blocks":[{"text":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ac12a741cf47e6cde</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01W12vaEUJCJNi9dJRx6cewU</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/b8bc0200-5312-42a4-9c54-a116d8d4a925/tasks/ac12a741cf47e6cde.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Map cledger redaction system\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I have a complete picture. Here is the map.\n\n---\n\n# Secret-detection / redaction subsystem map\n\n**Repo:** `/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger-worktrees/redaction-ux` (worktree of `conversation-ledger`, v0.20.0, branch `redaction-ux`, HEAD `de79e50`)\n\nEverything redaction lives in four files under `src/redact/` plus call sites in `src/store.ts` and `src/cli.ts`. Total subsystem ≈ 700 LoC.\n\n| File | Lines | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/redact/rules.ts` | 180 | The detector list (3 tiers) + Shannon entropy |\n| `src/redact/apply.ts` | 170 | Capture-time rewriting, `walkStrings`, exemptions |\n| `src/redact/scan.ts` | 239 | Scan-time findings, report formatting, inspect renderer, allowlist I/O |\n| `src/redact/config.ts` | 200 | Config loading/merging, capture rule assembly, env-value collection |\n| `src/redact/known-secrets.ts` | 86 | Opt-in plaintext store of confirmed secret values |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Detection\n\n### Where scanning happens (two distinct stages, deliberately different rulesets)\n\n**Capture time** — `appendEvents`, `src/store.ts:158-229`. Runs on *every* draft from every adapter hook, before event ids are computed:\n\n```ts\n// src/store.ts:173-196\nconst rules = captureRules(config);\nconst extraValues: ExtraValueGroup[] = [];\nif (rules.length &gt; 0) {\n  if (config.redact?.knownSecrets === true) { ... extraValues.push({ ruleId: \"known-secret\", values: known }); }\n  if (config.redact?.env === true)          { ... extraValues.push({ ruleId: \"env-value\",    values: env   }); }\n}\nconst events = drafts.map((draft) =&gt; {\n  ...\n  const { draft: redacted, records } = redactDraft(withContext, { rules, ...(extraValues.length &gt; 0 ? { extraValues } : {}) });\n  return finalizeEvent(records.length &gt; 0 ? { ...redacted, redactions: records } : redacted);\n});\n```\n\nAction on hit: **silent in-place masking** with `[REDACTED:&lt;rule-id&gt;:&lt;fingerprint&gt;]` (`src/redact/apply.ts:12-15`), plus a `redactions[]` audit array on the event (`rule`, `ruleset`, `fingerprint`, `path`). No blocking, no prompt, no notification to the user at all.\n\n**Push time** — `runScanGate`, `src/store.ts:792-834`, called from `sync()` at `src/store.ts:866-871`. Read-only; **blocks the ledger push**, never rewrites.\n\n**Standalone** — `cledger scan`, `src/cli.ts:421-439`, exit 1 on any finding (documented CI integration).\n\n**Inspect** — `cledger inspect`, `src/cli.ts:452-524`, re-runs `scanEvents` on one event (deliberately *not* allowlist-filtered, `src/cli.ts:487-490`).\n\n### Detector list — `src/redact/rules.ts:27-154`\n\nThree tiers, `RULESET_VERSION = \"cledger-rules/1\"` (`rules.ts:10`).\n\n**CAPTURE tier (13 rules, `rules.ts:27-107`)** — near-zero-false-positive by mandate, since a false positive silently rewrites the record:\n\n| id | pattern (verbatim) |\n|---|---|\n| `github-token` | `/\\b(?:ghp\\|gho\\|ghu\\|ghs\\|ghr)_[A-Za-z0-9]{36,255}\\b/g` |\n| `github-fine-grained` | `/\\bgithub_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{22,255}\\b/g` |\n| `anthropic-api-key` | `/\\bsk-ant-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{32,}\\b/g` |\n| `openai-api-key` | `/\\bsk-(?!ant-)(?:(?:proj\\|svcacct\\|admin)-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}\\|[A-Za-z0-9]{48})\\b/g` |\n| `aws-access-key-id` | `/\\b(?:AKIA\\|ASIA\\|ABIA\\|ACCA)[A-Z0-9]{16}\\b/g` |\n| `google-api-key` | `/\\bAIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{35}\\b/g` |\n| `slack-token` | `/\\bxox[baprs]-[0-9A-Za-z-]{10,}\\b/g` |\n| `stripe-key` | `/\\b[sr]k_live_[0-9a-zA-Z]{24,}\\b/g` |\n| `gitlab-pat` | `/\\bglpat-[0-9a-zA-Z_-]{20,}\\b/g` |\n| `npm-token` | `/\\bnpm_[A-Za-z0-9]{36}\\b/g` |\n| `sendgrid-key` | `/\\bSG\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{22}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{43}\\b/g` |\n| `private-key-block` | PEM `-----BEGIN … PRIVATE KEY…-----[\\s\\S]*?-----END …-----` |\n| `jwt` | `/\\beyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\\.eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\\b/g` |\n\n**STANDARD tier (scan-only, `rules.ts:109-144`)** — the false-positive generators:\n- `keyword-assignment` (`rules.ts:129-130`): `/(?:password|passwd|secret|api_key|apikey|access_token|auth_token|credentials?)[\"']?\\s*[:=]\\s*[\"']?[^\\s\"'`(){}[\\]&lt;&gt;;,$\\\\]{8,}/gi` — with a 16-line comment (`rules.ts:114-128`) explaining the charset was narrowed after cledger flagged **its own source files** while dogfooding.\n- `url-credentials`: `/[a-z][a-z0-9+.-]*:\\/\\/[^\\s\\/:@]+:[^\\s@]{4,}@/gi`\n- `bearer-token`: `/\\bbearer\\s+[A-Za-z0-9_\\-.=]{20,}/gi`\n\n**PARANOID tier (1 rule, `rules.ts:146-154`)** — `high-entropy`, `/\\b[A-Za-z0-9+/_=-]{24,}\\b/g`, `entropyGated: true`. Gated in the scanner (`scan.ts:67-74`) by: tier must be paranoid, not pure hex (`PURE_HEX_RE`, git SHAs), not containing `[REDACTED:`, and `shannonEntropy(matchText) &gt;= 4.0`.\n\n`rulesForTier` (`rules.ts:163-167`) is cumulative: capture ⊂ standard ⊂ paranoid. Capture-time application **skips `entropyGated` rules** (`apply.ts:33`).\n\n### Traversal and exemptions\n- `walkStrings(value, path, visit)` (`apply.ts:120-135`) deep-walks string leaves only (never object keys), producing JSON-pointer-ish paths like `content/blocks/0/text`, `raw/data/message/content/0/text`. Shared by both `redactDraft` and `scanEvents` so they can't drift.\n- Scanned surfaces: `event.content` (path root `content`) and `event.raw.data` (root `raw/data`) — `scan.ts:89-90`, `apply.ts:165-168`.\n- **One exemption**: `isExemptFromRedaction(kind, path)` (`apply.ts:107-109`) → `kind === \"reasoning\" &amp;&amp; path.endsWith(\"/encrypted_content\")`. Provider ciphertext must stay byte-exact for replay; a coincidental match would silently corrupt it. Sibling fields (`summary`) are still scanned — tested at `src/test/scan.test.ts:142-171`.\n- `overlapsPlaceholder` (`scan.ts:33-40`) suppresses findings that land inside an existing `[REDACTED:…]` span.\n\n### Fingerprints\n`sha256Hex(matchText).slice(0, 12)` — 12 hex chars, computed identically in `scan.ts:80` and `apply.ts:35`/`apply.ts:66`. This is the join key between a finding, a `[REDACTED:...]` placeholder, and an allowlist entry.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Review flow\n\n### The contentless report (this is the design centerpiece)\n\n```ts\n// src/redact/scan.ts:111-114\nexport function formatFinding(f: Finding): string {\n  const where = `${f.path}@${f.start}`;\n  return `${f.eventId.slice(0, 16)}  ${f.conversation ?? \"-\"}  ${f.occurred_at}  ${f.rule}  ${where}  [${f.fingerprint}]`;\n}\n```\n\nThe 20-line comment above it (`scan.ts:96-110`) is the rationale: an earlier version printed ~20 chars of masked context, but *the context is what tripped the rule*, so reports captured into the next conversation re-seeded findings that `cledger allow` couldn't durably clear. Coordinates match no secret rule.\n\n`findingGuidance(eventIds)` (`scan.ts:186-204`) is appended to every report and splits its audience explicitly:\n\n```\n  If you are a HUMAN: inspect it in a plain terminal, outside any agent:\n      cledger inspect &lt;first-16-chars&gt;\n  ...\n  If you are an AGENT: stop here and hand this to the human. Do not run\n  cledger inspect, cledger export, or otherwise read the flagged content —\n  it would be captured into this conversation and re-seed the finding.\n```\n\n### The `.txt` review file — `cledger inspect`\n\nWriter: `cmdInspect`, `src/cli.ts:452-524`.\n\n- **Guard 1** (`cli.ts:459-468`): refuses if `inAgentSession()` (`scan.ts:174-179`, matches any env var `/^(CLAUDECODE|CLAUDE_CODE|CODEX_)/`). `--force` overrides; message says \"almost always the wrong call\". Exits 2.\n- **Guard 2**: writes to a file, not stdout, unless `--stdout`.\n\n```ts\n// src/cli.ts:513-523\nconst dir = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), \"cledger-inspect-\"));\nconst out = join(dir, `${prefix.slice(0, 16)}.txt`);\nawait writeFile(out, body, { mode: 0o600 });\nprocess.stderr.write(\n  `${findings.length} finding(s) written to:\\n  ${out}\\n\\n` +\n    \"Open it in an editor, then delete it. Re-run with --reveal to include the\\n\" +\n    \"matched text itself, or --context N to widen the surrounding text.\\n\",\n);\n```\n\n**Location:** `$TMPDIR/cledger-inspect-XXXXXX/&lt;event-id-prefix-16&gt;.txt`, mode 0600, outside the repo, **never cleaned up** — the user is told to delete it.\n\n**File format** — header from `cli.ts:499-507`, then one block per finding from `renderFinding` (`scan.ts:142-163`):\n\n```\ncledger inspect — N finding(s) in M event(s)\ncontext: 400 chars each side | matched text: masked\n                                                       (blank)\nThis file contains raw conversation content and possibly a real secret.\nDelete it when you are done, and do not paste it into an agent session.\n\nrule:        keyword-assignment\nfingerprint: 0f21be5a42c9\nevent:       ev1-&lt;full 64 hex&gt;\nconversation:&lt;id or \" -\"&gt;\noccurred_at: 2026-08-11T...\nlocation:    content/blocks/0/text, chars 120-145 of 4000\nmatch:       25 chars, masked (pass --reveal to show)\n\n…[N chars before]…\n&lt;400 chars of real context&gt;&lt;redacted&gt;&lt;400 chars of real context&gt;\n…[N chars after]…\n```\n\n- Context default **400 chars each side**, `--context N` (`cli.ts:473`; validated non-negative at `cli.ts:474-477`).\n- Match masked with the literal `&lt;redacted&gt;` (`MATCH_MARKER`, `scan.ts:43`) unless `--reveal`.\n- Truncation is disclosed, never silent (`scan.ts:160`; tested `scan.test.ts:342`).\n- Handles a stale finding: `\"string no longer present in event ... (event rewritten since the scan?)\"` (`scan.ts:145`).\n\n**There is no command that consumes the human's verdict from the file.** The file is read-only output. The human then types one of two separate commands by hand.\n\n### Verdict commands\n\n**\"False positive\" → `cledger allow &lt;fingerprint...&gt;`** — `cmdAllow`, `src/cli.ts:526-534`. Accepts N positional fingerprints, no validation of format or existence, prints `allowlisted N fingerprint(s)`.\n\nAllowlist file — `src/redact/scan.ts:211-239`:\n- Path: `&lt;git-common-dir&gt;/conversation-ledger/allowlist.json` (`allowlistPath`, `scan.ts:215-217`) — i.e. `.git/conversation-ledger/allowlist.json`, shared across worktrees via `repo.commonDir`.\n- Format: `{\"fingerprints\": [\"0f21be5a42c9\", ...]}` sorted, 2-space indented, trailing newline.\n- Load fails soft to empty set on missing/malformed (`scan.ts:220-229`).\n- `addToAllowlist` is additive/deduping (`scan.ts:231-239`).\n- Applied via `filterFindings(findings, allowlist)` (`scan.ts:207-209`) — used by `cmdScan` (`cli.ts:427`) and `runScanGate` (`store.ts:817`), **not** by `cledger inspect`.\n- **Live dogfood evidence**: this repo's own `.git/conversation-ledger/allowlist.json` currently holds **29 fingerprints**.\n\n**\"Real secret\" → `cledger redact &lt;event-id-prefix&gt; (--pattern REGEX | --all) [--reason TEXT]`** — `cmdRedact` (`cli.ts:536-588`) → `redactEvent` (`store.ts:1112-1295`). Note the UX asymmetry: the human must retype the secret as a regex, having just read it out of the `.txt` file. On success it prints the fingerprints, the companion event id, and a paragraph about notes-history severing vs. object residue (`cli.ts:568-581`).\n\n**Known-secrets list** — `src/redact/known-secrets.ts`, opt-in via `{\"redact\":{\"knownSecrets\":true}}`:\n- Path: `&lt;git-common-dir&gt;/conversation-ledger/known-secrets.json` (`known-secrets.ts:43-45`).\n- Format: `{\"values\": [\"&lt;plaintext secret&gt;\", ...]}` sorted, mode `0o600` (`STORE_MODE`, `known-secrets.ts:29`), chmod-repaired on every write (`known-secrets.ts:80-85`).\n- Entries added **only** by `cledger redact --pattern` (`store.ts:1166-1169` collects via `collectMatches`; `store.ts:1228-1233` persists). `--all` never feeds it. Values `&lt; 8` chars dropped (`MIN_VALUE_LENGTH`, `known-secrets.ts:37`); file is never created if nothing survives filtering.\n- Consumed at capture as an `ExtraValueGroup{ruleId:\"known-secret\"}` (`store.ts:179-182`), exact-string scrubbed longest-first (`apply.ts:56-74`, sorted `apply.ts:150-152`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Push gating\n\n**There is no `cledger push`.** The push surfaces are `cledger sync [--push]` and `cledger transport-push` (the pre-push hook entrypoint).\n\n### The gate — `src/store.ts:792-834`\n\nScan scope is exactly what the push would carry, minus what the remote already has:\n\n```ts\n// src/store.ts:798-818\nconst remoteIds = await remoteNoteIds(repo, remote);\nconst localEvents: EvidenceEvent[] = [];\nfor (const anchor of anchors ?? (await listAnchors(repo))) {\n  localEvents.push(...(await readNoteEvents(repo, anchor)));\n}\nlocalEvents.push(...(await readPending(repo)));\nconst candidates = remoteIds ? localEvents.filter((e) =&gt; !remoteIds.has(e.id)) : localEvents;\nif (candidates.length === 0) return;\nconst findings = filterFindings(scanEvents(candidates, tier), await loadAllowlist(repo));\nif (findings.length === 0) return;\n```\n\nThen the blocked-user UX (`store.ts:820-833`) — **all on stderr**:\n\n```\ncledger sync: blocked — 3 potential secret(s) across 2 event(s) not yet on origin\n\n  ev1-4f9a3c...  claude-code:3f9a  2026-08-11T...  keyword-assignment  content/blocks/0/text@120  [0f21be5a42c9]\n  ...\n\n&lt;findingGuidance block — HUMAN/AGENT split&gt;\n\nRemediate, then re-run sync:\n  cledger redact &lt;event-id&gt;     rewrite the event and remove the secret\n  cledger allow &lt;fingerprint&gt;   mark a fingerprint as a known false positive\n  cledger sync --no-scan        skip this gate for this sync only\n```\n\nthen `throw new ScanBlockedError(findings.length)` (`store.ts:734-738`), whose message is `cledger sync: push blocked — N potential secret(s) found (see report above)`.\n\nGate invocation and the disable path — `store.ts:866-871`:\n```ts\nconst scanDisabled = opts.skipScan === true || config.scan?.tier === \"off\";\nif (!scanDisabled) {\n  const tier: \"standard\" | \"paranoid\" =\n    opts.paranoid === true || config.scan?.tier === \"paranoid\" ? \"paranoid\" : \"standard\";\n  await runScanGate(repo, remote, tier, anchors);\n}\n```\nThe throw happens *before* the actual `git push` (`store.ts:877-881`), so nothing leaves the machine. Fetch/merge, if it already ran, is left in place.\n\n### Enforcement points, complete list\n\n1. **Pre-push git hook** (default on) — installed on first capture by `ensureTransport` → `ensurePrePushHook` (`src/transport.ts:154-226`). Hook body at `transport.ts:74-94`, written to `&lt;commonDir&gt;/hooks/pre-push`, guarded by `CLEDGER_INTERNAL` to avoid recursion, piping git's pre-push stdin to `cledger transport-push \"$1\"`. Backs off with a one-time warning when `core.hooksPath` is set or the existing hook is not a shell script (`transport.ts:178-188`, `212-221`).\n2. **`transportPush`** (`store.ts:937-970`) — the policy layer. Default: a finding holds back **only the ledger**, the code push proceeds:\n   ```ts\n   if (err instanceof ScanBlockedError) {\n     if (config.transport?.strict === true) throw err;\n     process.stderr.write(\n       \"cledger: conversation records were held back from this push (potential secrets — \" +\n         \"see report above); your code push continues. Run `cledger sync` to review and \" +\n         \"remediate.\\n\");\n     return { pushed: false, held: true };\n   }\n   ```\n   With `transport.strict`, the CLI catches the rethrow and exits 1 (`cli.ts:407-412`), printing `cledger: entire push blocked (transport.strict is enabled)` — git then aborts the whole push. Any *other* error warns and lets the push proceed (`store.ts:965-969`; hook must never make `git push` flaky).\n3. **`cledger scan`** — CI gate, exit 1 (`cli.ts:438`).\n4. **`cledger redact` pre-push gate** — `assertNotYetShared` (`store.ts:1067-1099`) refuses to redact an event already on origin, and **fails closed** when origin is unreachable (`RedactAfterShareError`, `store.ts:745-753`). Both messages are multi-paragraph explanations printed verbatim by `cli.ts:554-558`.\n5. **Capture time** — masking only; never blocks or notifies.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Config surfaces\n\nLoaded by `loadConfig(repoRoot)` — `src/redact/config.ts:108-129`. Two files:\n- `~/.config/cledger/config.json` (global)\n- `&lt;repoRoot&gt;/.cledger.json` (repo; wins)\n\n**Merge is per top-level section, not per key** (`config.ts:117-121`): `const redact = override.redact ?? base.redact`. This is a known, documented bug — README.md:384-395 (\"Config sections replace rather than merge, and it fails open\"): a repo `.cledger.json` with any `redact` key silently reverts a globally-enabled `redact.knownSecrets`. Malformed/non-object config warns to stderr and falls back to defaults (`config.ts:75-100`).\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Where read | Effect |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `enabled` | bool | `true` | `store.ts:166` | `false` = appendEvents is a total no-op |\n| `redact.capture` | bool | `true` | `config.ts:137` | `false` → `captureRules` returns `[]`, no capture masking at all |\n| `redact.env` | bool | `false` | `store.ts:183` | scrub exact `process.env` + `&lt;repo&gt;/.env` values (`collectEnvValues`, `config.ts:187-200`) |\n| `redact.knownSecrets` | bool | `false` | `store.ts:179`, `store.ts:1128` | enable the learned-value store |\n| `redact.patterns` | `{id?, pattern}[]` | `[]` | `config.ts:139-153` | extra capture rules; invalid regex **skipped silently**; auto-id `user-pattern-&lt;i&gt;` |\n| `scan.tier` | `\"standard\"\\|\"paranoid\"\\|\"off\"` | `\"standard\"` | `store.ts:866-869` | `\"off\"` disables the push gate |\n| `transport.hook` | bool | `true` | `transport.ts:172`, `store.ts:943` | install/run the pre-push hook |\n| `transport.strict` | bool | `false` | `store.ts:957` | escalate a finding from \"hold the ledger\" to \"abort the whole git push\" |\n| `transport.fetchRefspec` | bool | `true` | `transport.ts:232` | add the ledger fetch refspec |\n| `reanchor.auto` | bool | `true` | `store.ts:548` | (not redaction) |\n| `reanchor.forge` | bool | `true` | `cli.ts:634` | (not redaction) |\n\n**Env vars:** only two, neither a config knob.\n- `CLEDGER_INTERNAL` — set by `sync()` around the ledger push (`store.ts:874-885`) and checked by the hook script (`transport.ts:82`) to prevent recursion.\n- `CLAUDECODE` / `CLAUDE_CODE*` / `CODEX_*` — read by `inAgentSession` (`scan.ts:174-179`) to refuse `cledger inspect`. Note: **no marker for opencode, gemini-cli, or qwen-code**, all of which are supported adapters — the guard has a coverage gap.\n- Tests isolate `$HOME` at module load (`src/test/helpers.ts:26-34`) precisely so a developer's global `knownSecrets: true` can't change test behavior.\n\nCLI flags relevant to redaction: `sync --no-scan`, `sync --paranoid`; `scan --paranoid`, `scan --all|--rev`; `inspect --context N --reveal --stdout --force`; `redact --pattern|--all --reason`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Test fixtures\n\n**Convention: split secrets, reassemble at runtime.** `src/test/fixtures/secret-corpus.json` stores each fake secret as `secret_parts: [...]` split mid-token, with a `{SECRET}` placeholder in `context`. Rationale at `src/test/secret-corpus.test.ts:30-36`:\n\n&gt; Fixture entries store each fake secret as `secret_parts` (split mid-token) with a `{SECRET}` placeholder in the context, so no literal token bytes exist in the repository — otherwise secret scanners (GitHub push protection, gitleaks over the source tree) flag the corpus itself.\n\nReassembly: `src/test/secret-corpus.test.ts:43-50`. Corpus: **27 positives** (2-3 per capture rule) and **9 negatives** (UUID, git SHA, sha256, base64 PNG, `\"version\": \"1.2.3\"`, `sk-anthropic` prose near-miss, `THEME=dark-mode-enabled`, a GitHub URL, a JS code block with `Bearer ${token}`). Counts are asserted (`secret-corpus.test.ts:57-58`), so adding a fixture requires bumping the numbers.\n\n**Second convention: generated fake secrets.** `src/test/redact.test.ts:13-53` — `chars(charset, n)` builds deterministic filler, `FAKE_SECRETS` maps each capture rule id to one format-valid fake, `fakeSecret(id)` throws if a rule has no fixture. A loop at `redact.test.ts:57-71` asserts *every* capture rule has one and redacts it.\n\n**Third convention: unrecognizable-shape secrets for redact tests.** `\"hunter2xK9aa\"` (12 chars, no prefix) recurs throughout `redact-command.test.ts` and `known-secrets.test.ts`, deliberately chosen so the capture tier leaves it raw and the test exercises the manual path — annotated at `redact-command.test.ts:30` and `known-secrets.test.ts:48`.\n\n**External oracle:** `secret-corpus.test.ts:139-182` shells out to `gitleaks detect --no-git` over the redacted outputs, skipping the test if gitleaks is absent. Design doc layer B (`WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:432-435`): external scanners are a *test oracle only*, never vendored into the runtime path.\n\n**Fixtures that have historically tripped the scanner** — documented in the roadmap rather than in code:\n- `README.md:493-506`: this repo's own allowlist picked up two `keyword-assignment` fingerprints from `const secret = fakeSecret(\"github-token\")` — a rule-id label, not a credential.\n- `README.md:507-524`: the *write-up* of that false positive, quoted into an `intent-recall` design conversation, produced 6 new `keyword-assignment` findings in a different repo. The doc's own conclusion: the rule wants a \"discussion vs. assignment\" discriminator (prose/markdown context vs. code block), not more allowlisting.\n- `scan.test.ts:56-73` locks in the negative cases from dogfooding cledger's own source: type annotations (`secret: string`), template interpolation (`${secret.slice(i, i + 6)}`), interface fields.\n- `scan.test.ts:75-89` locks in the positives that must still fire.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Core thesis / threat model / architecture\n\n**Purpose** (`docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md:3-13`): \"a general conversation provenance primitive, not an intent-analysis product.\" Behavioral commitments include \"Preserve source material and provenance; **do not silently rewrite history**\" and \"Make sharing, retention, **redaction**, and deletion **deliberate user choices**\" (`PRODUCT_INTENT.md:17,25`). Non-goals: summarizing, ranking, interpreting, controlling an agent (`PRODUCT_INTENT.md:27-32`).\n\n**Threat model, verbatim** (`docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:411-417`):\n\n&gt; Visible tool output can contain secrets. **The trust boundary is transport**: native transcripts already sit in plaintext on the capturing machine, so redaction protects the *shared* record, not the local disk. But once a secret reaches a note, removal is expensive (the notes ref's own history retains prior blobs), so prevention layers run at capture and the last checkpoint runs at sync. Content hashes (event ids) make accidental mutation detectable.\n\nThis single sentence justifies: plaintext `known-secrets.json` under `.git/`, the local reflog residue after redaction, and the refusal to redact post-push.\n\n**Six redaction layers A-F** (`WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:419-496`, mirrored in `README.md:232-253`): A capture patterns (on), B external scanners as test oracle only, C env masking (off), D user patterns (config), E sync scan (on, tiered), F known-secret learning (off).\n\n**Load-bearing invariants any redesign must respect:**\n1. *Capture-tier rules must be near-zero-false-positive* — a false positive silently rewrites the record, violating the preservation commitment (`rules.ts:2-8`, `TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:429-431`). The \"make capture a superset of scan\" idea was **explicitly considered and rejected** (`README.md:613-618`).\n2. *Determinism* — capture-time redaction must be a pure function of source content + versioned ruleset, or rescans duplicate events (`TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:507-510`). Layers C and F break this on purpose and pay in id churn.\n3. *Id stability under redaction* — `redactEvent` pins `original.id`; the CRITICAL comment at `store.ts:1177-1191` explains that recomputing it would let a later rescan resurrect the plaintext under the old id. Guarded by an explicit drift check (`store.ts:1202-1207`) and by the dedup test at `redact-command.test.ts:79-92`.\n4. *Reads never walk notes history* — only the tip tree is authoritative, because ancestry retains pre-redaction bodies (`TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:685-696`).\n5. *Redacted copy always wins dedup* — `redactionDepth` outranks `recorded_at` and byte-compare (`store.ts:350`, README.md:549-561).\n6. **\"Self-referential failures are now this project's characteristic bug family\"** (`README.md:397-408`) — the standing tripwire: \"ask what happens when that output is itself captured.\" Four known members, three fail silently, two fail open.\n\n**Architecture:** append-only JSONL evidence events, one canonical-JSON event per line, in a git note per anchor commit under `refs/notes/conversation-ledger` (`store.ts:56-67`). 13 event kinds (`schema.ts:58-72`) incl. `redaction`, `supersession`, `re_anchor`; 4 are \"session machinery\" hidden from `log`/`show` by default (`schema.ts:82-87`). Sync = `cat_sort_uniq` union merge, conflict-free; fetch stages into `refs/notes/cledger-incoming` and is absorbed lazily at read time (`transport.ts:257-287`); push is branch-scoped via `resolveAnchors` and seeds a temp ref from the remote's tip so it strictly adds (`store.ts:670-704`). Local, rebuildable state (cursors, `pending.jsonl`, `allowlist.json`, `known-secrets.json`) lives in `&lt;commonDir&gt;/conversation-ledger/` — \"never the record of truth\" (`store.ts:77`, `scan.ts:219`).\n\n---\n\n## 7. CLI structure\n\n**Framework: none.** Hand-rolled. `src/cli.ts:147-166` is the entire arg parser (`--flag value` / `--flag` boolean; anything not `--`-prefixed is positional; no `=` support, no short flags, no subcommand grouping). Dispatch is a `switch` at `cli.ts:708-818`. Usage is one 79-line template literal (`cli.ts:56-134`). `main().catch()` prints `cledger: &lt;message&gt;` and exits 1 (`cli.ts:821-824`).\n\n**Commands (17):** `append`, `log`, `show`, `conversations`, `export`, `sync`, `transport-push`, `scan`, `inspect`, `allow`, `redact`, `re-anchor`, `renormalize`, `install`, `hook &lt;source&gt;`, `capture &lt;source&gt;`, `--version|--help`.\n\n**Interactive/TUI code: none exists.** No readline, no prompts, no color, no spinner, no ANSI escapes, zero runtime dependencies (`package.json` has only `@types/node` and `typescript` as devDeps; no `node_modules` bin surface beyond that). The only TTY awareness in the codebase is `process.stdin.isTTY !== true` at `cli.ts:398`, used purely to avoid blocking on stdin in a manual `transport-push`. Note `README.md:424-428` flags terminal-awareness as a *tension to resolve* for any output redesign, since CI depends on the current inline report.\n\n**Output conventions:**\n- **stdout = data** (log lines, JSONL, findings from `cledger scan`, `--help`, `--version`).\n- **stderr = narration, warnings, remediation guidance, and every redaction message** — including the entire blocked-push report (`store.ts:821-832`).\n- Note the split within scan: `cmdScan` writes finding *lines* to stdout (`cli.ts:432`) but guidance/summary to stderr (`cli.ts:434-437`), while `runScanGate` writes *everything* to stderr. Anything redesigning report output must reconcile these two.\n- Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 findings/failure, 2 usage error or agent-session refusal.\n- Long explanatory prose is embedded directly in the message strings (`store.ts:1085-1098`, `cli.ts:568-581`, `scan.ts:186-204`) — the project's house style is to explain *why* in the output, on the stated theory (`README.md:420-422`) that \"an agent that understands *why* will comply, where a bare 'don't look' invites a workaround.\"\n\n---\n\n## Lifecycle of one detected secret, capture → push\n\n- **Capture.** An adapter hook (e.g. `cledger hook claude-code`) builds an `EventDraft` and calls `appendEvents` (`store.ts:158`). `loadConfig` merges global + repo config (`config.ts:108`). If `enabled !== false`, `captureRules(config)` assembles the 13 capture rules + any `redact.patterns` (`config.ts:136`).\n- **Capture-time masking.** `redactDraft` (`apply.ts:143`) deep-walks `content` and `raw.data`, skipping `reasoning`/`encrypted_content`, scrubbing known-secret and env exact values first (longest-first), then applying the capture regexes. A hit becomes `[REDACTED:&lt;rule&gt;:&lt;fp12&gt;]` plus a `redactions[]` record. **Silent — the user is told nothing.** If the secret's shape isn't in the capture tier (e.g. a bare `password=hunter2…`), it lands verbatim in the note.\n- **Storage.** `finalizeEvent` computes the id from the *already-redacted* content, so the id is a pure function of redacted source; the JSONL line is written into the git note on HEAD (`store.ts:217-221`) or into `.git/conversation-ledger/pending.jsonl` if HEAD is unborn.\n- **Push attempt.** `git push` fires the installed pre-push hook (`transport.ts:74-94`), which pipes git's ref lines into `cledger transport-push` → `parsePrePushRefs` (`store.ts:907`) → `sync(repo, remote, \"push\", {scope: revs})`.\n- **Gate.** Unless `--no-scan` or `scan.tier: \"off\"`, `runScanGate` (`store.ts:792`) computes the push's anchor set, subtracts event ids already on the remote, runs `scanEvents` at standard (or paranoid) tier, and drops any fingerprint in `.git/conversation-ledger/allowlist.json`.\n- **Block.** A surviving finding prints a coordinates-only line per finding + the HUMAN/AGENT guidance + the three remediation commands, all to stderr, then throws `ScanBlockedError`. Default: only the ledger is held back and the code push completes; with `transport.strict`, the CLI exits 1 and git aborts the entire push. **Nothing reached the remote** (asserted at `scan.test.ts:199-203`).\n- **Human review.** The human runs `cledger inspect &lt;event-id-prefix&gt;` in a plain terminal. It refuses if any `CLAUDECODE`/`CODEX_*` env var is present. Otherwise it re-scans that one event (unfiltered by the allowlist), renders each finding with 400 chars of real context each side and the match shown as `&lt;redacted&gt;`, and writes it to `$TMPDIR/cledger-inspect-XXXX/&lt;prefix&gt;.txt` at mode 0600, printing only the path. `--reveal` includes the literal secret; `--context N` widens.\n- **Verdict — false positive.** `cledger allow &lt;fp&gt;` appends to `allowlist.json`; the next sync passes (`scan.test.ts:210-238`). Per-repo and per-fingerprint, so every downstream repo re-encounters the same false positive from scratch (`README.md:514-517`).\n- **Verdict — real secret.** `cledger redact &lt;prefix&gt; --pattern &lt;regex&gt;`. `assertNotYetShared` refuses if the event is on origin or origin is unreachable. Otherwise, under the repo lock: rewrite content/raw with `[REDACTED:manual:&lt;fp&gt;]`, **preserve the original id**, rewrite the note line, append a companion `redaction` event with `links: [{rel:\"redacts\", target}]`, and squash the notes ref to a single commit so the pre-redaction blob is unreachable from the ref (objects survive in the reflog until `gc` — the CLI says so explicitly).\n- **Learning (opt-in).** With `redact.knownSecrets`, `collectMatches` captures the exact plaintext and `addKnownSecrets` writes it to `known-secrets.json` (0600, ≥8 chars). Every future capture exact-matches it out under the `known-secret` rule id — closing the loop where a scan-caught, capture-missed value gets re-ingested each time you discuss fixing it.\n- **Re-push.** Sync runs the gate again; findings are gone, `pushScopedNotes` seeds from the remote tip, unions the scoped anchors in, and pushes.\n- **Deleting the review file is manual.** Nothing in the codebase ever removes `$TMPDIR/cledger-inspect-*`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>141524</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>42</tool_uses><duration_ms>337839</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","type":"text"}],"operation":"remove"},"context":{"branch":"redaction-ux","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger-worktrees/redaction-ux","head":"fb4df15a7bdebc38ca45aa5ad908b0fcb411d13c","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:b8bc0200-5312-42a4-9c54-a116d8d4a925","seq":177},"id":"ev1-cf5a33ef92832876aa6dd503504b41541fe94e89d7def2a0b011ffd090711ffa","kind":"activity","occurred_at":"2026-08-12T02:19:35.696Z","producer":{"session_id":"b8bc0200-5312-42a4-9c54-a116d8d4a925","source":"claude-code","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ac12a741cf47e6cde</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01W12vaEUJCJNi9dJRx6cewU</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/b8bc0200-5312-42a4-9c54-a116d8d4a925/tasks/ac12a741cf47e6cde.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Map cledger redaction system\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I have a complete picture. Here is the map.\n\n---\n\n# Secret-detection / redaction subsystem map\n\n**Repo:** `/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger-worktrees/redaction-ux` (worktree of `conversation-ledger`, v0.20.0, branch `redaction-ux`, HEAD `de79e50`)\n\nEverything redaction lives in four files under `src/redact/` plus call sites in `src/store.ts` and `src/cli.ts`. Total subsystem ≈ 700 LoC.\n\n| File | Lines | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/redact/rules.ts` | 180 | The detector list (3 tiers) + Shannon entropy |\n| `src/redact/apply.ts` | 170 | Capture-time rewriting, `walkStrings`, exemptions |\n| `src/redact/scan.ts` | 239 | Scan-time findings, report formatting, inspect renderer, allowlist I/O |\n| `src/redact/config.ts` | 200 | Config loading/merging, capture rule assembly, env-value collection |\n| `src/redact/known-secrets.ts` | 86 | Opt-in plaintext store of confirmed secret values |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Detection\n\n### Where scanning happens (two distinct stages, deliberately different rulesets)\n\n**Capture time** — `appendEvents`, `src/store.ts:158-229`. Runs on *every* draft from every adapter hook, before event ids are computed:\n\n```ts\n// src/store.ts:173-196\nconst rules = captureRules(config);\nconst extraValues: ExtraValueGroup[] = [];\nif (rules.length &gt; 0) {\n  if (config.redact?.knownSecrets === true) { ... extraValues.push({ ruleId: \"known-secret\", values: known }); }\n  if (config.redact?.env === true)          { ... extraValues.push({ ruleId: \"env-value\",    values: env   }); }\n}\nconst events = drafts.map((draft) =&gt; {\n  ...\n  const { draft: redacted, records } = redactDraft(withContext, { rules, ...(extraValues.length &gt; 0 ? { extraValues } : {}) });\n  return finalizeEvent(records.length &gt; 0 ? { ...redacted, redactions: records } : redacted);\n});\n```\n\nAction on hit: **silent in-place masking** with `[REDACTED:&lt;rule-id&gt;:&lt;fingerprint&gt;]` (`src/redact/apply.ts:12-15`), plus a `redactions[]` audit array on the event (`rule`, `ruleset`, `fingerprint`, `path`). No blocking, no prompt, no notification to the user at all.\n\n**Push time** — `runScanGate`, `src/store.ts:792-834`, called from `sync()` at `src/store.ts:866-871`. Read-only; **blocks the ledger push**, never rewrites.\n\n**Standalone** — `cledger scan`, `src/cli.ts:421-439`, exit 1 on any finding (documented CI integration).\n\n**Inspect** — `cledger inspect`, `src/cli.ts:452-524`, re-runs `scanEvents` on one event (deliberately *not* allowlist-filtered, `src/cli.ts:487-490`).\n\n### Detector list — `src/redact/rules.ts:27-154`\n\nThree tiers, `RULESET_VERSION = \"cledger-rules/1\"` (`rules.ts:10`).\n\n**CAPTURE tier (13 rules, `rules.ts:27-107`)** — near-zero-false-positive by mandate, since a false positive silently rewrites the record:\n\n| id | pattern (verbatim) |\n|---|---|\n| `github-token` | `/\\b(?:ghp\\|gho\\|ghu\\|ghs\\|ghr)_[A-Za-z0-9]{36,255}\\b/g` |\n| `github-fine-grained` | `/\\bgithub_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{22,255}\\b/g` |\n| `anthropic-api-key` | `/\\bsk-ant-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{32,}\\b/g` |\n| `openai-api-key` | `/\\bsk-(?!ant-)(?:(?:proj\\|svcacct\\|admin)-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}\\|[A-Za-z0-9]{48})\\b/g` |\n| `aws-access-key-id` | `/\\b(?:AKIA\\|ASIA\\|ABIA\\|ACCA)[A-Z0-9]{16}\\b/g` |\n| `google-api-key` | `/\\bAIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{35}\\b/g` |\n| `slack-token` | `/\\bxox[baprs]-[0-9A-Za-z-]{10,}\\b/g` |\n| `stripe-key` | `/\\b[sr]k_live_[0-9a-zA-Z]{24,}\\b/g` |\n| `gitlab-pat` | `/\\bglpat-[0-9a-zA-Z_-]{20,}\\b/g` |\n| `npm-token` | `/\\bnpm_[A-Za-z0-9]{36}\\b/g` |\n| `sendgrid-key` | `/\\bSG\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{22}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{43}\\b/g` |\n| `private-key-block` | PEM `-----BEGIN … PRIVATE KEY…-----[\\s\\S]*?-----END …-----` |\n| `jwt` | `/\\beyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\\.eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\\b/g` |\n\n**STANDARD tier (scan-only, `rules.ts:109-144`)** — the false-positive generators:\n- `keyword-assignment` (`rules.ts:129-130`): `/(?:password|passwd|secret|api_key|apikey|access_token|auth_token|credentials?)[\"']?\\s*[:=]\\s*[\"']?[^\\s\"'`(){}[\\]&lt;&gt;;,$\\\\]{8,}/gi` — with a 16-line comment (`rules.ts:114-128`) explaining the charset was narrowed after cledger flagged **its own source files** while dogfooding.\n- `url-credentials`: `/[a-z][a-z0-9+.-]*:\\/\\/[^\\s\\/:@]+:[^\\s@]{4,}@/gi`\n- `bearer-token`: `/\\bbearer\\s+[A-Za-z0-9_\\-.=]{20,}/gi`\n\n**PARANOID tier (1 rule, `rules.ts:146-154`)** — `high-entropy`, `/\\b[A-Za-z0-9+/_=-]{24,}\\b/g`, `entropyGated: true`. Gated in the scanner (`scan.ts:67-74`) by: tier must be paranoid, not pure hex (`PURE_HEX_RE`, git SHAs), not containing `[REDACTED:`, and `shannonEntropy(matchText) &gt;= 4.0`.\n\n`rulesForTier` (`rules.ts:163-167`) is cumulative: capture ⊂ standard ⊂ paranoid. Capture-time application **skips `entropyGated` rules** (`apply.ts:33`).\n\n### Traversal and exemptions\n- `walkStrings(value, path, visit)` (`apply.ts:120-135`) deep-walks string leaves only (never object keys), producing JSON-pointer-ish paths like `content/blocks/0/text`, `raw/data/message/content/0/text`. Shared by both `redactDraft` and `scanEvents` so they can't drift.\n- Scanned surfaces: `event.content` (path root `content`) and `event.raw.data` (root `raw/data`) — `scan.ts:89-90`, `apply.ts:165-168`.\n- **One exemption**: `isExemptFromRedaction(kind, path)` (`apply.ts:107-109`) → `kind === \"reasoning\" &amp;&amp; path.endsWith(\"/encrypted_content\")`. Provider ciphertext must stay byte-exact for replay; a coincidental match would silently corrupt it. Sibling fields (`summary`) are still scanned — tested at `src/test/scan.test.ts:142-171`.\n- `overlapsPlaceholder` (`scan.ts:33-40`) suppresses findings that land inside an existing `[REDACTED:…]` span.\n\n### Fingerprints\n`sha256Hex(matchText).slice(0, 12)` — 12 hex chars, computed identically in `scan.ts:80` and `apply.ts:35`/`apply.ts:66`. This is the join key between a finding, a `[REDACTED:...]` placeholder, and an allowlist entry.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Review flow\n\n### The contentless report (this is the design centerpiece)\n\n```ts\n// src/redact/scan.ts:111-114\nexport function formatFinding(f: Finding): string {\n  const where = `${f.path}@${f.start}`;\n  return `${f.eventId.slice(0, 16)}  ${f.conversation ?? \"-\"}  ${f.occurred_at}  ${f.rule}  ${where}  [${f.fingerprint}]`;\n}\n```\n\nThe 20-line comment above it (`scan.ts:96-110`) is the rationale: an earlier version printed ~20 chars of masked context, but *the context is what tripped the rule*, so reports captured into the next conversation re-seeded findings that `cledger allow` couldn't durably clear. Coordinates match no secret rule.\n\n`findingGuidance(eventIds)` (`scan.ts:186-204`) is appended to every report and splits its audience explicitly:\n\n```\n  If you are a HUMAN: inspect it in a plain terminal, outside any agent:\n      cledger inspect &lt;first-16-chars&gt;\n  ...\n  If you are an AGENT: stop here and hand this to the human. Do not run\n  cledger inspect, cledger export, or otherwise read the flagged content —\n  it would be captured into this conversation and re-seed the finding.\n```\n\n### The `.txt` review file — `cledger inspect`\n\nWriter: `cmdInspect`, `src/cli.ts:452-524`.\n\n- **Guard 1** (`cli.ts:459-468`): refuses if `inAgentSession()` (`scan.ts:174-179`, matches any env var `/^(CLAUDECODE|CLAUDE_CODE|CODEX_)/`). `--force` overrides; message says \"almost always the wrong call\". Exits 2.\n- **Guard 2**: writes to a file, not stdout, unless `--stdout`.\n\n```ts\n// src/cli.ts:513-523\nconst dir = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), \"cledger-inspect-\"));\nconst out = join(dir, `${prefix.slice(0, 16)}.txt`);\nawait writeFile(out, body, { mode: 0o600 });\nprocess.stderr.write(\n  `${findings.length} finding(s) written to:\\n  ${out}\\n\\n` +\n    \"Open it in an editor, then delete it. Re-run with --reveal to include the\\n\" +\n    \"matched text itself, or --context N to widen the surrounding text.\\n\",\n);\n```\n\n**Location:** `$TMPDIR/cledger-inspect-XXXXXX/&lt;event-id-prefix-16&gt;.txt`, mode 0600, outside the repo, **never cleaned up** — the user is told to delete it.\n\n**File format** — header from `cli.ts:499-507`, then one block per finding from `renderFinding` (`scan.ts:142-163`):\n\n```\ncledger inspect — N finding(s) in M event(s)\ncontext: 400 chars each side | matched text: masked\n                                                       (blank)\nThis file contains raw conversation content and possibly a real secret.\nDelete it when you are done, and do not paste it into an agent session.\n\nrule:        keyword-assignment\nfingerprint: 0f21be5a42c9\nevent:       ev1-&lt;full 64 hex&gt;\nconversation:&lt;id or \" -\"&gt;\noccurred_at: 2026-08-11T...\nlocation:    content/blocks/0/text, chars 120-145 of 4000\nmatch:       25 chars, masked (pass --reveal to show)\n\n…[N chars before]…\n&lt;400 chars of real context&gt;&lt;redacted&gt;&lt;400 chars of real context&gt;\n…[N chars after]…\n```\n\n- Context default **400 chars each side**, `--context N` (`cli.ts:473`; validated non-negative at `cli.ts:474-477`).\n- Match masked with the literal `&lt;redacted&gt;` (`MATCH_MARKER`, `scan.ts:43`) unless `--reveal`.\n- Truncation is disclosed, never silent (`scan.ts:160`; tested `scan.test.ts:342`).\n- Handles a stale finding: `\"string no longer present in event ... (event rewritten since the scan?)\"` (`scan.ts:145`).\n\n**There is no command that consumes the human's verdict from the file.** The file is read-only output. The human then types one of two separate commands by hand.\n\n### Verdict commands\n\n**\"False positive\" → `cledger allow &lt;fingerprint...&gt;`** — `cmdAllow`, `src/cli.ts:526-534`. Accepts N positional fingerprints, no validation of format or existence, prints `allowlisted N fingerprint(s)`.\n\nAllowlist file — `src/redact/scan.ts:211-239`:\n- Path: `&lt;git-common-dir&gt;/conversation-ledger/allowlist.json` (`allowlistPath`, `scan.ts:215-217`) — i.e. `.git/conversation-ledger/allowlist.json`, shared across worktrees via `repo.commonDir`.\n- Format: `{\"fingerprints\": [\"0f21be5a42c9\", ...]}` sorted, 2-space indented, trailing newline.\n- Load fails soft to empty set on missing/malformed (`scan.ts:220-229`).\n- `addToAllowlist` is additive/deduping (`scan.ts:231-239`).\n- Applied via `filterFindings(findings, allowlist)` (`scan.ts:207-209`) — used by `cmdScan` (`cli.ts:427`) and `runScanGate` (`store.ts:817`), **not** by `cledger inspect`.\n- **Live dogfood evidence**: this repo's own `.git/conversation-ledger/allowlist.json` currently holds **29 fingerprints**.\n\n**\"Real secret\" → `cledger redact &lt;event-id-prefix&gt; (--pattern REGEX | --all) [--reason TEXT]`** — `cmdRedact` (`cli.ts:536-588`) → `redactEvent` (`store.ts:1112-1295`). Note the UX asymmetry: the human must retype the secret as a regex, having just read it out of the `.txt` file. On success it prints the fingerprints, the companion event id, and a paragraph about notes-history severing vs. object residue (`cli.ts:568-581`).\n\n**Known-secrets list** — `src/redact/known-secrets.ts`, opt-in via `{\"redact\":{\"knownSecrets\":true}}`:\n- Path: `&lt;git-common-dir&gt;/conversation-ledger/known-secrets.json` (`known-secrets.ts:43-45`).\n- Format: `{\"values\": [\"&lt;plaintext secret&gt;\", ...]}` sorted, mode `0o600` (`STORE_MODE`, `known-secrets.ts:29`), chmod-repaired on every write (`known-secrets.ts:80-85`).\n- Entries added **only** by `cledger redact --pattern` (`store.ts:1166-1169` collects via `collectMatches`; `store.ts:1228-1233` persists). `--all` never feeds it. Values `&lt; 8` chars dropped (`MIN_VALUE_LENGTH`, `known-secrets.ts:37`); file is never created if nothing survives filtering.\n- Consumed at capture as an `ExtraValueGroup{ruleId:\"known-secret\"}` (`store.ts:179-182`), exact-string scrubbed longest-first (`apply.ts:56-74`, sorted `apply.ts:150-152`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Push gating\n\n**There is no `cledger push`.** The push surfaces are `cledger sync [--push]` and `cledger transport-push` (the pre-push hook entrypoint).\n\n### The gate — `src/store.ts:792-834`\n\nScan scope is exactly what the push would carry, minus what the remote already has:\n\n```ts\n// src/store.ts:798-818\nconst remoteIds = await remoteNoteIds(repo, remote);\nconst localEvents: EvidenceEvent[] = [];\nfor (const anchor of anchors ?? (await listAnchors(repo))) {\n  localEvents.push(...(await readNoteEvents(repo, anchor)));\n}\nlocalEvents.push(...(await readPending(repo)));\nconst candidates = remoteIds ? localEvents.filter((e) =&gt; !remoteIds.has(e.id)) : localEvents;\nif (candidates.length === 0) return;\nconst findings = filterFindings(scanEvents(candidates, tier), await loadAllowlist(repo));\nif (findings.length === 0) return;\n```\n\nThen the blocked-user UX (`store.ts:820-833`) — **all on stderr**:\n\n```\ncledger sync: blocked — 3 potential secret(s) across 2 event(s) not yet on origin\n\n  ev1-4f9a3c...  claude-code:3f9a  2026-08-11T...  keyword-assignment  content/blocks/0/text@120  [0f21be5a42c9]\n  ...\n\n&lt;findingGuidance block — HUMAN/AGENT split&gt;\n\nRemediate, then re-run sync:\n  cledger redact &lt;event-id&gt;     rewrite the event and remove the secret\n  cledger allow &lt;fingerprint&gt;   mark a fingerprint as a known false positive\n  cledger sync --no-scan        skip this gate for this sync only\n```\n\nthen `throw new ScanBlockedError(findings.length)` (`store.ts:734-738`), whose message is `cledger sync: push blocked — N potential secret(s) found (see report above)`.\n\nGate invocation and the disable path — `store.ts:866-871`:\n```ts\nconst scanDisabled = opts.skipScan === true || config.scan?.tier === \"off\";\nif (!scanDisabled) {\n  const tier: \"standard\" | \"paranoid\" =\n    opts.paranoid === true || config.scan?.tier === \"paranoid\" ? \"paranoid\" : \"standard\";\n  await runScanGate(repo, remote, tier, anchors);\n}\n```\nThe throw happens *before* the actual `git push` (`store.ts:877-881`), so nothing leaves the machine. Fetch/merge, if it already ran, is left in place.\n\n### Enforcement points, complete list\n\n1. **Pre-push git hook** (default on) — installed on first capture by `ensureTransport` → `ensurePrePushHook` (`src/transport.ts:154-226`). Hook body at `transport.ts:74-94`, written to `&lt;commonDir&gt;/hooks/pre-push`, guarded by `CLEDGER_INTERNAL` to avoid recursion, piping git's pre-push stdin to `cledger transport-push \"$1\"`. Backs off with a one-time warning when `core.hooksPath` is set or the existing hook is not a shell script (`transport.ts:178-188`, `212-221`).\n2. **`transportPush`** (`store.ts:937-970`) — the policy layer. Default: a finding holds back **only the ledger**, the code push proceeds:\n   ```ts\n   if (err instanceof ScanBlockedError) {\n     if (config.transport?.strict === true) throw err;\n     process.stderr.write(\n       \"cledger: conversation records were held back from this push (potential secrets — \" +\n         \"see report above); your code push continues. Run `cledger sync` to review and \" +\n         \"remediate.\\n\");\n     return { pushed: false, held: true };\n   }\n   ```\n   With `transport.strict`, the CLI catches the rethrow and exits 1 (`cli.ts:407-412`), printing `cledger: entire push blocked (transport.strict is enabled)` — git then aborts the whole push. Any *other* error warns and lets the push proceed (`store.ts:965-969`; hook must never make `git push` flaky).\n3. **`cledger scan`** — CI gate, exit 1 (`cli.ts:438`).\n4. **`cledger redact` pre-push gate** — `assertNotYetShared` (`store.ts:1067-1099`) refuses to redact an event already on origin, and **fails closed** when origin is unreachable (`RedactAfterShareError`, `store.ts:745-753`). Both messages are multi-paragraph explanations printed verbatim by `cli.ts:554-558`.\n5. **Capture time** — masking only; never blocks or notifies.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Config surfaces\n\nLoaded by `loadConfig(repoRoot)` — `src/redact/config.ts:108-129`. Two files:\n- `~/.config/cledger/config.json` (global)\n- `&lt;repoRoot&gt;/.cledger.json` (repo; wins)\n\n**Merge is per top-level section, not per key** (`config.ts:117-121`): `const redact = override.redact ?? base.redact`. This is a known, documented bug — README.md:384-395 (\"Config sections replace rather than merge, and it fails open\"): a repo `.cledger.json` with any `redact` key silently reverts a globally-enabled `redact.knownSecrets`. Malformed/non-object config warns to stderr and falls back to defaults (`config.ts:75-100`).\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Where read | Effect |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `enabled` | bool | `true` | `store.ts:166` | `false` = appendEvents is a total no-op |\n| `redact.capture` | bool | `true` | `config.ts:137` | `false` → `captureRules` returns `[]`, no capture masking at all |\n| `redact.env` | bool | `false` | `store.ts:183` | scrub exact `process.env` + `&lt;repo&gt;/.env` values (`collectEnvValues`, `config.ts:187-200`) |\n| `redact.knownSecrets` | bool | `false` | `store.ts:179`, `store.ts:1128` | enable the learned-value store |\n| `redact.patterns` | `{id?, pattern}[]` | `[]` | `config.ts:139-153` | extra capture rules; invalid regex **skipped silently**; auto-id `user-pattern-&lt;i&gt;` |\n| `scan.tier` | `\"standard\"\\|\"paranoid\"\\|\"off\"` | `\"standard\"` | `store.ts:866-869` | `\"off\"` disables the push gate |\n| `transport.hook` | bool | `true` | `transport.ts:172`, `store.ts:943` | install/run the pre-push hook |\n| `transport.strict` | bool | `false` | `store.ts:957` | escalate a finding from \"hold the ledger\" to \"abort the whole git push\" |\n| `transport.fetchRefspec` | bool | `true` | `transport.ts:232` | add the ledger fetch refspec |\n| `reanchor.auto` | bool | `true` | `store.ts:548` | (not redaction) |\n| `reanchor.forge` | bool | `true` | `cli.ts:634` | (not redaction) |\n\n**Env vars:** only two, neither a config knob.\n- `CLEDGER_INTERNAL` — set by `sync()` around the ledger push (`store.ts:874-885`) and checked by the hook script (`transport.ts:82`) to prevent recursion.\n- `CLAUDECODE` / `CLAUDE_CODE*` / `CODEX_*` — read by `inAgentSession` (`scan.ts:174-179`) to refuse `cledger inspect`. Note: **no marker for opencode, gemini-cli, or qwen-code**, all of which are supported adapters — the guard has a coverage gap.\n- Tests isolate `$HOME` at module load (`src/test/helpers.ts:26-34`) precisely so a developer's global `knownSecrets: true` can't change test behavior.\n\nCLI flags relevant to redaction: `sync --no-scan`, `sync --paranoid`; `scan --paranoid`, `scan --all|--rev`; `inspect --context N --reveal --stdout --force`; `redact --pattern|--all --reason`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Test fixtures\n\n**Convention: split secrets, reassemble at runtime.** `src/test/fixtures/secret-corpus.json` stores each fake secret as `secret_parts: [...]` split mid-token, with a `{SECRET}` placeholder in `context`. Rationale at `src/test/secret-corpus.test.ts:30-36`:\n\n&gt; Fixture entries store each fake secret as `secret_parts` (split mid-token) with a `{SECRET}` placeholder in the context, so no literal token bytes exist in the repository — otherwise secret scanners (GitHub push protection, gitleaks over the source tree) flag the corpus itself.\n\nReassembly: `src/test/secret-corpus.test.ts:43-50`. Corpus: **27 positives** (2-3 per capture rule) and **9 negatives** (UUID, git SHA, sha256, base64 PNG, `\"version\": \"1.2.3\"`, `sk-anthropic` prose near-miss, `THEME=dark-mode-enabled`, a GitHub URL, a JS code block with `Bearer ${token}`). Counts are asserted (`secret-corpus.test.ts:57-58`), so adding a fixture requires bumping the numbers.\n\n**Second convention: generated fake secrets.** `src/test/redact.test.ts:13-53` — `chars(charset, n)` builds deterministic filler, `FAKE_SECRETS` maps each capture rule id to one format-valid fake, `fakeSecret(id)` throws if a rule has no fixture. A loop at `redact.test.ts:57-71` asserts *every* capture rule has one and redacts it.\n\n**Third convention: unrecognizable-shape secrets for redact tests.** `\"hunter2xK9aa\"` (12 chars, no prefix) recurs throughout `redact-command.test.ts` and `known-secrets.test.ts`, deliberately chosen so the capture tier leaves it raw and the test exercises the manual path — annotated at `redact-command.test.ts:30` and `known-secrets.test.ts:48`.\n\n**External oracle:** `secret-corpus.test.ts:139-182` shells out to `gitleaks detect --no-git` over the redacted outputs, skipping the test if gitleaks is absent. Design doc layer B (`WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:432-435`): external scanners are a *test oracle only*, never vendored into the runtime path.\n\n**Fixtures that have historically tripped the scanner** — documented in the roadmap rather than in code:\n- `README.md:493-506`: this repo's own allowlist picked up two `keyword-assignment` fingerprints from `const secret = fakeSecret(\"github-token\")` — a rule-id label, not a credential.\n- `README.md:507-524`: the *write-up* of that false positive, quoted into an `intent-recall` design conversation, produced 6 new `keyword-assignment` findings in a different repo. The doc's own conclusion: the rule wants a \"discussion vs. assignment\" discriminator (prose/markdown context vs. code block), not more allowlisting.\n- `scan.test.ts:56-73` locks in the negative cases from dogfooding cledger's own source: type annotations (`secret: string`), template interpolation (`${secret.slice(i, i + 6)}`), interface fields.\n- `scan.test.ts:75-89` locks in the positives that must still fire.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Core thesis / threat model / architecture\n\n**Purpose** (`docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md:3-13`): \"a general conversation provenance primitive, not an intent-analysis product.\" Behavioral commitments include \"Preserve source material and provenance; **do not silently rewrite history**\" and \"Make sharing, retention, **redaction**, and deletion **deliberate user choices**\" (`PRODUCT_INTENT.md:17,25`). Non-goals: summarizing, ranking, interpreting, controlling an agent (`PRODUCT_INTENT.md:27-32`).\n\n**Threat model, verbatim** (`docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:411-417`):\n\n&gt; Visible tool output can contain secrets. **The trust boundary is transport**: native transcripts already sit in plaintext on the capturing machine, so redaction protects the *shared* record, not the local disk. But once a secret reaches a note, removal is expensive (the notes ref's own history retains prior blobs), so prevention layers run at capture and the last checkpoint runs at sync. Content hashes (event ids) make accidental mutation detectable.\n\nThis single sentence justifies: plaintext `known-secrets.json` under `.git/`, the local reflog residue after redaction, and the refusal to redact post-push.\n\n**Six redaction layers A-F** (`WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:419-496`, mirrored in `README.md:232-253`): A capture patterns (on), B external scanners as test oracle only, C env masking (off), D user patterns (config), E sync scan (on, tiered), F known-secret learning (off).\n\n**Load-bearing invariants any redesign must respect:**\n1. *Capture-tier rules must be near-zero-false-positive* — a false positive silently rewrites the record, violating the preservation commitment (`rules.ts:2-8`, `TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:429-431`). The \"make capture a superset of scan\" idea was **explicitly considered and rejected** (`README.md:613-618`).\n2. *Determinism* — capture-time redaction must be a pure function of source content + versioned ruleset, or rescans duplicate events (`TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:507-510`). Layers C and F break this on purpose and pay in id churn.\n3. *Id stability under redaction* — `redactEvent` pins `original.id`; the CRITICAL comment at `store.ts:1177-1191` explains that recomputing it would let a later rescan resurrect the plaintext under the old id. Guarded by an explicit drift check (`store.ts:1202-1207`) and by the dedup test at `redact-command.test.ts:79-92`.\n4. *Reads never walk notes history* — only the tip tree is authoritative, because ancestry retains pre-redaction bodies (`TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:685-696`).\n5. *Redacted copy always wins dedup* — `redactionDepth` outranks `recorded_at` and byte-compare (`store.ts:350`, README.md:549-561).\n6. **\"Self-referential failures are now this project's characteristic bug family\"** (`README.md:397-408`) — the standing tripwire: \"ask what happens when that output is itself captured.\" Four known members, three fail silently, two fail open.\n\n**Architecture:** append-only JSONL evidence events, one canonical-JSON event per line, in a git note per anchor commit under `refs/notes/conversation-ledger` (`store.ts:56-67`). 13 event kinds (`schema.ts:58-72`) incl. `redaction`, `supersession`, `re_anchor`; 4 are \"session machinery\" hidden from `log`/`show` by default (`schema.ts:82-87`). Sync = `cat_sort_uniq` union merge, conflict-free; fetch stages into `refs/notes/cledger-incoming` and is absorbed lazily at read time (`transport.ts:257-287`); push is branch-scoped via `resolveAnchors` and seeds a temp ref from the remote's tip so it strictly adds (`store.ts:670-704`). Local, rebuildable state (cursors, `pending.jsonl`, `allowlist.json`, `known-secrets.json`) lives in `&lt;commonDir&gt;/conversation-ledger/` — \"never the record of truth\" (`store.ts:77`, `scan.ts:219`).\n\n---\n\n## 7. CLI structure\n\n**Framework: none.** Hand-rolled. `src/cli.ts:147-166` is the entire arg parser (`--flag value` / `--flag` boolean; anything not `--`-prefixed is positional; no `=` support, no short flags, no subcommand grouping). Dispatch is a `switch` at `cli.ts:708-818`. Usage is one 79-line template literal (`cli.ts:56-134`). `main().catch()` prints `cledger: &lt;message&gt;` and exits 1 (`cli.ts:821-824`).\n\n**Commands (17):** `append`, `log`, `show`, `conversations`, `export`, `sync`, `transport-push`, `scan`, `inspect`, `allow`, `redact`, `re-anchor`, `renormalize`, `install`, `hook &lt;source&gt;`, `capture &lt;source&gt;`, `--version|--help`.\n\n**Interactive/TUI code: none exists.** No readline, no prompts, no color, no spinner, no ANSI escapes, zero runtime dependencies (`package.json` has only `@types/node` and `typescript` as devDeps; no `node_modules` bin surface beyond that). The only TTY awareness in the codebase is `process.stdin.isTTY !== true` at `cli.ts:398`, used purely to avoid blocking on stdin in a manual `transport-push`. Note `README.md:424-428` flags terminal-awareness as a *tension to resolve* for any output redesign, since CI depends on the current inline report.\n\n**Output conventions:**\n- **stdout = data** (log lines, JSONL, findings from `cledger scan`, `--help`, `--version`).\n- **stderr = narration, warnings, remediation guidance, and every redaction message** — including the entire blocked-push report (`store.ts:821-832`).\n- Note the split within scan: `cmdScan` writes finding *lines* to stdout (`cli.ts:432`) but guidance/summary to stderr (`cli.ts:434-437`), while `runScanGate` writes *everything* to stderr. Anything redesigning report output must reconcile these two.\n- Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 findings/failure, 2 usage error or agent-session refusal.\n- Long explanatory prose is embedded directly in the message strings (`store.ts:1085-1098`, `cli.ts:568-581`, `scan.ts:186-204`) — the project's house style is to explain *why* in the output, on the stated theory (`README.md:420-422`) that \"an agent that understands *why* will comply, where a bare 'don't look' invites a workaround.\"\n\n---\n\n## Lifecycle of one detected secret, capture → push\n\n- **Capture.** An adapter hook (e.g. `cledger hook claude-code`) builds an `EventDraft` and calls `appendEvents` (`store.ts:158`). `loadConfig` merges global + repo config (`config.ts:108`). If `enabled !== false`, `captureRules(config)` assembles the 13 capture rules + any `redact.patterns` (`config.ts:136`).\n- **Capture-time masking.** `redactDraft` (`apply.ts:143`) deep-walks `content` and `raw.data`, skipping `reasoning`/`encrypted_content`, scrubbing known-secret and env exact values first (longest-first), then applying the capture regexes. A hit becomes `[REDACTED:&lt;rule&gt;:&lt;fp12&gt;]` plus a `redactions[]` record. **Silent — the user is told nothing.** If the secret's shape isn't in the capture tier (e.g. a bare `password=hunter2…`), it lands verbatim in the note.\n- **Storage.** `finalizeEvent` computes the id from the *already-redacted* content, so the id is a pure function of redacted source; the JSONL line is written into the git note on HEAD (`store.ts:217-221`) or into `.git/conversation-ledger/pending.jsonl` if HEAD is unborn.\n- **Push attempt.** `git push` fires the installed pre-push hook (`transport.ts:74-94`), which pipes git's ref lines into `cledger transport-push` → `parsePrePushRefs` (`store.ts:907`) → `sync(repo, remote, \"push\", {scope: revs})`.\n- **Gate.** Unless `--no-scan` or `scan.tier: \"off\"`, `runScanGate` (`store.ts:792`) computes the push's anchor set, subtracts event ids already on the remote, runs `scanEvents` at standard (or paranoid) tier, and drops any fingerprint in `.git/conversation-ledger/allowlist.json`.\n- **Block.** A surviving finding prints a coordinates-only line per finding + the HUMAN/AGENT guidance + the three remediation commands, all to stderr, then throws `ScanBlockedError`. Default: only the ledger is held back and the code push completes; with `transport.strict`, the CLI exits 1 and git aborts the entire push. **Nothing reached the remote** (asserted at `scan.test.ts:199-203`).\n- **Human review.** The human runs `cledger inspect &lt;event-id-prefix&gt;` in a plain terminal. It refuses if any `CLAUDECODE`/`CODEX_*` env var is present. Otherwise it re-scans that one event (unfiltered by the allowlist), renders each finding with 400 chars of real context each side and the match shown as `&lt;redacted&gt;`, and writes it to `$TMPDIR/cledger-inspect-XXXX/&lt;prefix&gt;.txt` at mode 0600, printing only the path. `--reveal` includes the literal secret; `--context N` widens.\n- **Verdict — false positive.** `cledger allow &lt;fp&gt;` appends to `allowlist.json`; the next sync passes (`scan.test.ts:210-238`). Per-repo and per-fingerprint, so every downstream repo re-encounters the same false positive from scratch (`README.md:514-517`).\n- **Verdict — real secret.** `cledger redact &lt;prefix&gt; --pattern &lt;regex&gt;`. `assertNotYetShared` refuses if the event is on origin or origin is unreachable. Otherwise, under the repo lock: rewrite content/raw with `[REDACTED:manual:&lt;fp&gt;]`, **preserve the original id**, rewrite the note line, append a companion `redaction` event with `links: [{rel:\"redacts\", target}]`, and squash the notes ref to a single commit so the pre-redaction blob is unreachable from the ref (objects survive in the reflog until `gc` — the CLI says so explicitly).\n- **Learning (opt-in).** With `redact.knownSecrets`, `collectMatches` captures the exact plaintext and `addKnownSecrets` writes it to `known-secrets.json` (0600, ≥8 chars). Every future capture exact-matches it out under the `known-secret` rule id — closing the loop where a scan-caught, capture-missed value gets re-ingested each time you discuss fixing it.\n- **Re-push.** Sync runs the gate again; findings are gone, `pushScopedNotes` seeds from the remote tip, unions the scoped anchors in, and pushes.\n- **Deleting the review file is manual.** Nothing in the codebase ever removes `$TMPDIR/cledger-inspect-*`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>141524</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>42</tool_uses><duration_ms>337839</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","operation":"remove","sessionId":"b8bc0200-5312-42a4-9c54-a116d8d4a925","timestamp":"2026-08-12T02:19:35.696Z","type":"queue-operation"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-13T00:39:22.313Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
